    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation following the codebase's existing pattern for response-only derived fields (`locality`, `contactPreference`, etc.), keeping each changed unit small and cohesive.\n\n**Files touched (5), each change minimal:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (contract, no code) \u2014 added `birthDate` (date) to `OwnerFields` and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated DTOs gain `getBirthDate`/`setAgeBand`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` column with a trivial getter/setter (CC 1 each). MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` from the request DTO onto the entity, so the flat-file registration echo pattern (like `registrationDate`) carries it.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one new `@AfterMapping default deriveAgeBand(...)` method (CC 4) alongside the sibling derive methods. It computes whole years via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` and picks `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`, leaving the field unset when no birth date is given.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column (only the hsqldb schema carries these evolution columns; h2 uses `ddl-auto=update`, and mysql/postgres are already stale for the other added columns, so I left them as-is to match convention).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the 10 positional seed inserts to match the new column count.\n\n**Structural-impact considerations:** No existing method was grown \u2014 the age-band logic lives in a single new small method with low surrounding complexity, and the entity change is just plain accessors. I confirmed the derivation must persist `birthDate` (the check happens on a separate `GET`), so storing it and deriving at map time is the lowest-impact placement that keeps `ageBand` non-persistent and consistent with the other derived response fields.",
